{number: 6}
{title: Praise to the Lord, the Almighty}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Praise to the [C] Lord, the Al-[Dm] mighty, the [Bb] King of cre-[C] a-[F] tion!
[F] O my soul, [C] praise Him, for [Dm] He is thy [Bb] health and sal-[C] va-[F] tion!
[F] All ye who [C] hear, [F] now to His [Bb] temple draw [C] near;
[Dm] Join me in [Bb] glad ado-[C] ra-[F] tion!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Praise to the [C] Lord, Who o'er [Dm] all things so [Bb] wondrously [C] reign-[F] eth,
[F] Shelters thee [C] under His [Dm] wings, yea, so [Bb] gently sus-[C] tain-[F] eth!
[F] Hast thou not [C] seen [F] how thy de-[Bb] sires e'er have [C] been
[Dm] Granted in [Bb] what He or-[C] dain-[F] eth?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Praise to the [C] Lord, Who doth [Dm] prosper thy [Bb] work and de-[C] fend [F] thee;
[F] Surely His [C] goodness and [Dm] mercy here [Bb] daily at-[C] tend [F] thee:
[F] Ponder a-[C] new [F] what the Al-[Bb] mighty can [C] do,
[Dm] If with His [Bb] love He be-[C] friend [F] thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] Praise to the [C] Lord, O let [Dm] all that is [Bb] in me a-[C] dore [F] Him!
[F] All that hath [C] life and breath, [Dm] come now with [Bb] praises be-[C] fore [F] Him!
[F] Let the A-[C] men [F] sound from His [Bb] people a-[C] gain;
[Dm] Gladly for [Bb] aye we a-[C] dore [F] Him.
{end_of_verse}
